WEBVTT

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:04.640
That mannerism... Are you Saturn-san?

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.930
You became young?

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.100
Huh? What?

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:10.760
The blast might have blown 
everyone to Galapagos.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:22.160
Heaven's Design Team

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.860
Everyone, are you okay?!

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:56.630
Mars-san and the person from the 
insect department are kids!

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.340
So small!

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:02.500
It looks like we got younger when 
the time accelerator exploded.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.130
Did the same thing happen 
to the others, too?

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:08.260
What are the current settings for Galapagos?

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:13.950
Well, Pluto-chan was testing her piranhas
 after they got accepted, so it's a jungle.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.820
They're all stuck in this 
jungle as children!

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.820
Th-This is bad! We have to find them quick!

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.910
Wait, Shimoda-kun.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:25.650
Galapagos is full of dangers right now!

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:30.660
Instead of just running into it blindly,
 we need to have a plan.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.200
A plan, huh?

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:38.080
That reminds me. I think Jupiter-kun pocketed
some of those bean paste buns you made.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:44.530
If everything caught in the blast has regressed,
 those bean paste buns might have, too.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:48.310
Even if they did, 
how will dough help us?

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.420
No, no. Even further back.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.650
That white bean paste is made 
from lima beans, right?

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.800
When lima beans are attacked 
by their natural enemy,

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.450
they emit this "Help me!" odor, right?

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:03.170
Didn't the insect department make an 
insect that can detect that smell?

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.330
Yes, very impressive!

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:08.870
We created a carnivorous 
insect that loves to eat

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.630
the herbivorous insect that 
eats the lima bean leaves.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.450
When this insect notices 
the lima bean's SOS signal,

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:15.830
it rushes to the plant and eats the 
insect nibbling on the lima bean.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:16.840
<b>Lima Bean</b>

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:18.480
That looks yummy.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:20.320
Someone help!

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:19.840
<b>Herbivore</b>

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.330
I'm <i>bean</i>' eaten!

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.840
That voice belongs to...

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:24.850
<b>Carnivore</b>

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:27.130
Yay, food!

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:29.830
I meant to feast, but now I'm the feast!

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.860
All according to plan!

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:34.700
That sounds like a convoluted revenge drama.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.270
It's a mite, by the way.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.230
<b>Phytoseiulus
 persimilis</b>

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.530
We'll make a detector that 
uses this mite sensor.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.480
Yeah!

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:46.130
But the SOS signal won't be emitted 
unless the bean is being eaten, right?

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:48.460
I'm not sure Jupiter-san 
would eat the plant's beans

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:51.010
just because the bean paste bun 
suddenly turned into one.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:52.480
I think he would.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.670
In a flash.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:57.520
Can this be eaten? When you're pondering that
 is the best time to eat!

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:58.870
He <i>would</i> eat them.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.640
The Bean Being Eaten Sensor is done!

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:02.850
That was fast!

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.220
It's saying he's over there!

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.650
He's eating already?

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:10.270
Mars-kun, please go back and fix 
the time accelerator device.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:11.100
Roger that!

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.640
You guys!

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:22.280
Jupiter-kun!

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:23.900
He really was eating them.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.910
Chief, you're so young!

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:27.720
Look who's talking.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.770
We came to rescue you. 
Where are the others?

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:34.430
I got stuck in this tree, 
but the others were blown that way.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.190
I heard some water, so they 
might be in the pond.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:38.160
Pond?

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.200
Probably the one for testing the piranhas.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.680
Let's hurry!

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.840
Pluto-chan, this pond...

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:51.890
I filled it with piranhas!

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.250
Please, no! We'll get attacked!

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.400
Hey! If you move—

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.970
I hear children's voices!

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:03.020
Over there!

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.110
P-P-Pluto-chan, are you okay?

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:09.480
It's fine.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:12.320
These piranhas are vegetarians!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.910
<b>Metynnis
 argenteus</b>

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.020
Vegetarian piranhas?!

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:19.100
Yes. Since they look like the 
vicious carnivorous piranhas,

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.660
they are less likely to be 
attacked by other fish.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:25.640
Huh? This fin has been bitten 
by a carnivorous piranha.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:29.040
So there are carnivorous ones in here!

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:33.150
It's fine. The carnivorous piranhas 
often don't kill their prey.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.560
Instead, they just eat a part of the fin.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.630
That's because the fins regenerate.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:41.130
Piranhas are creatures that 
treat resources with respect.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:42.310
I see...

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:46.260
So if you're not too frilly, 
you won't get nibbled on so much.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:47.860
Frilly?

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:50.570
We need to get out of here quick.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:53.200
Let's get on this leaf for now.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.580
<b>Victoria
 amazonica</b>

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.730
Good thing we're kids.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:58.040
Our adult bodies would've weighed too much.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:01.870
Piranhas don't go 
out of their way to attack,

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:04.350
but avoid splashing around just to be safe.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:06.550
Ven-chan, what's that you have there?

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.530
Oh, this is—

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:12.970
Jeez! She just said 
to not splash around!

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:13.710
I'm sorry.

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.320
Be careful, sheesh.

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:17.170
I'm really sorry, you guys.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:21.720
I forgot that I added the piranhas' 
natural enemy to help the test go better.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.610
Namely, crocodiles.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.730
Why would you do that?!

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.000
Quick, over here!

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:41.500
This might be the end.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:49.560
J-Just eat this!

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:56.040
Nice pitch!

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.820
L-Look! It's working?!

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:00.150
What was that?

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:03.220
This is cassava root, the source of tapioca!

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:05.940
The tapioca in the bubble tea
 I had when we were eating

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.900
Shimoda-kun's bean paste buns
 has regressed, too.

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:11.480
Before it's processed, cassava root
 contains a cyanogenic compound.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:14.360
It's a neurotoxin like potassium cyanide!

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.790
Eat tapioca!

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.580
<b>Float...</b>

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.340
Nice aim! You sank a lot of them!

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:26.330
But I'm all out of cassava roots now!

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:28.700
There are still so many of them!

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:32.720
Mercury, those are your crocodiles.
 Do something!

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.710
I'm already on it!

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:39.490
Crocodiles are highly sociable 
creatures that communicate vocally.

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:42.240
So that's why I'm going to cry now!

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:48.310
What's that?

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:50.660
Oh, it's a sound to shoo them away.

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:52.050
There's no such sound.

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:55.730
This is the sound a baby crocodile 
makes to call for its mother.

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:03.160
One of them is coming here.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.080
The one who responded is a female.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.240
What will bringing her here do?!

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:10.240
The female will come close. And then...

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:16.260
<b>Female</b>

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:16.260
<b>Male</b>

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:13.610
<i>Hey, what do you want with my wife?</i>

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:16.260
<b>Male</b>

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:16.270
<i>What are you talking about, you idiot?</i>

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:19.280
<i>You won't lay even one finger on my wife!</i>

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:21.970
<i>You're all going to die!</i>

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:23.650
<i>Ow! What's your problem!?</i>

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:26.700
The husband crocodile is 
chasing the other ones away!

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:28.650
It's a huge brawl!

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.650
Where are you going?! Stop!

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:32.660
All right, they swam away!

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:36.770
W-Wait, there's one left here! 
That female from before.

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:39.180
She's looking at us with this

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.520
"you'll make good food for my 
children" kind of expression!

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.530
It's okay. If it's just one, we can manage!

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:50.660
If possible, I didn't want to create this,
 but I have no choice.

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:56.860
Goodbye, my cute otter.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:01.170
This is the order I'm currently working on!

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:06.140
An "otter that's not cute at all"!

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:10.150
God has spoken!

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:12.340
Accepted!

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:14.400
<b>Accepted</b>

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.400
<b>Giant Otter</b>

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:18.270
Oh, Shimoda-kun! Over here!

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.870
We're here! Over here!

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:22.350
You guys!

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:28.270
Oh, boy! I'm glad nobody got hurt.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.200
You used to be so cute.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:35.050
He's so big and scary now.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:38.300
The insect department came 
to help, too? Thanks.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.300
We solved everything by ourselves, though.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:44.420
We rushed over when we heard the screams,
 but you guys were amazing.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:47.300
Thanks to that, I had a good idea.

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:50.050
What do you think of an insect 
that screams for help?

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:52.320
<b>Honey</b>

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:54.500
Usually it secretes honey 
and is friends with ants.

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:56.210
You can eat my honey.

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:57.320
Yay!

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.750
A larva. I'm ready to eat!

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:01.520
When it's about to be attacked—

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:04.910
Ahhh!

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.910
Our honey buddy is in danger!

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.200
To the rescue!

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:09.050
Wait, this was inspired by us?

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:11.200
God has spoken!

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:13.280
Accepted!

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:15.340
<b>Accepted</b>

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:15.340
<b>Gossamer-Winged
 Butterfly Larva</b>

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:15.330
Yay!

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:17.930
I'll go back to the insect department
 and make it right away!

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.340
Good luck!

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.650
The time acceleration device is fixed 
as well, so all is back to normal.

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:25.060
I'm just glad nobody got hurt.

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:29.950
Being young isn't bad every now and then, 
but my current body suits me the best.

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:33.530
Whatever happened to that stuck goat?

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:35.290
The magic circle is gone, too.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:37.290
Looks like it made it to Hell in one piece.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:38.720
I'm glad to hear that.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:39.530
<b>Cassava
 Root</b>

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:46.140
Oh, the sample from the design team!

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:47.030
Huh?

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:53.220
Why is its torso so long?

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:58.280
Maybe it's a transmission error? Or...

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:03.180
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:01.830
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:07.450
I always pictured them as attacking in 
a swarm, but you say they're cowards?

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:10.060
Yes, they form swarms 
because they're scared.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:13.750
If something big falls in the water, 
they run away most of the time.

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:16.670
Doesn't "most of the time" mean
 they also attack sometimes?

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:20.840
If the prey is hurt, they get excited 
by the scent of blood and might attack.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:22.550
So they do attack!

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:27.200
They're only really known for their bite, 
but there's something I want you to know.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:29.700
Piranhas can speak!

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:31.690
Speak? How?

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:33.940
They use their swim bladder to make sounds.

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:35.560
It sounds kind of like, "Boof"!

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:37.820
I think it'll do it when 
you grab it. Want to try?

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:42.340
Before I do that, I want to 
know why it makes that sound.

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.100
To warn you that it's about to bite.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.790
I knew it was all about biting!

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:58.370
We don't get many opportunities 
to put on dazzling makeup like this.

00:11:58.370 --> 00:11:59.860
It's kind of fun.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.250
All right, ready to go!

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:10.490
What's wrong?

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:14.150
Neptune-san is saying he won't be 
attending today's party in Hell.

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:15.960
What? You're not coming?

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:19.460
I already told them we're all coming, though.

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:20.830
What's the matter?

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:24.340
Well, I'm in a slump.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:29.220
I'm not making any progress with this 
order for a "fluffy but spiky animal."

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:32.360
The more I hurry, the more 
wrong turns I take.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:35.360
By now, I don't even feel 
like holding my pen.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.540
But I have to do something...

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:39.310
That's why I can't join you.

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:41.120
Another mystery order?

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:42.940
I feel for you.

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:45.950
Why don't you say you're not feeling 
well and get a deadline extension?

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:47.120
Then you can go to the party.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:50.450
I heard Hell is outside of 
Heaven's reception range.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.240
You do have to unwind sometimes.

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:56.900
Shimoda-kun, please report that 
Neptune-san's submission will be delayed

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:58.680
because he's not feeling well.
 Lay it on thick!

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:00.370
I-Is that okay?

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:03.390
A slump is a form of not 
feeling well, right?

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:04.750
It's fine, isn't it?

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:06.630
Then it's settled.

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:08.540
Let's go!

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.390
Welcome to Hell.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:26.300
Let me greet you among 
with the wails of joy.

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:32.780
Now, let us begin the banquet to celebrate 
the founding of Hell's sales team!

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:36.050
You will get a real taste of Hell!

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:39.040
<b><u>A Word From the Chef</u>
\hHee hee hee!
\hTurn this into
\h\hyour own flesh
\h\h\hand blood...</b>

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:39.040
Turn this into your own flesh and blood!

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:42.040
That's what our company's chef says.

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:46.040
Please enjoy everything until you 
have far surpassed being full.

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:48.250
Not to sound cliché, but...

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:49.800
We're being wined and dined here.

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:51.800
Cheers!

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:55.000
You shouldn't have done 
all this for just us.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.430
It's nothing. Besides, we'll keep
 relying on your services.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:14:01.300
Huh, so this is Hell's main door.

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:02.770
It's flashier than ours.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:05.700
We all brought you gifts for the occasion.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:08.940
Oh, that's so considerate. Thank you!

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:12.900
We thought that you would 
like something like this.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:16.940
What is that?! It's like a symbol 
of destruction!

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:19.190
That's so freaking cool!

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:21.950
I'm glad that it was up your alley.

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:23.540
This is from me.

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:27.120
A snake skeleton!

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.220
<b>Snake Skeleton
</b>(For Decorative Use)

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:28.220
So cool!

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:31.810
Wow, everything below the 
head is vertebrae, right?!

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:35.690
Actually, while they don't stand out so much,
there's a neck and a tail, too.

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:37.770
<b>Neck</b>

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:37.770
<b>Tail</b>

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:37.760
Snakes have quite a short neck.

00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:41.370
I brought a giant chicken skull.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:45.230
<b>Chicken Skull
</b>(For Costume Use)

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:43.140
That's so cool!

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:45.230
You can wear it.

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:48.230
Wh-What do you think?

00:14:48.230 --> 00:14:50.710
Do I look like the Prince of Madness?

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:52.740
It looks great on you. Wonderful!

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:56.160
That ring by the eyes... Is that bone?

00:14:56.160 --> 00:15:00.630
Chickens have bones that maintain
 the shape of their eyes.

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:02.650
This is from me.

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:04.910
Another oblong box.

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:07.020
Oh, I know what this is.

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:08.580
This is an anteater!

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:09.890
Correct!

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.050
All the way to the tip 
of their mouth is bone!

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:13.390
<b>Anteater Skull
</b> (For Decorative Use)

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:15.280
I brought this—

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:16.560
A horse, right?

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:17.750
Yes, why?

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.630
Incidentally, do you think this 
is a male or female horse?

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:22.390
Isn't that question too hard?

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:24.490
It's actually quite easy.

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:26.980
The ones that have sharp 
teeth here are male.

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:30.500
They have canines for when they 
fight to secure their female.

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:32.410
Horses are quite strong, you know?

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:35.320
This one's from me.

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:36.410
That's big!

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:40.290
This... This was...

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:43.540
A cyclops!

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.080
So cool!

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:47.930
No, this was an elephant.

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:52.430
The hole in the middle wasn't for 
an eyeball. It was for the nose.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:53.520
The eyes are over here.

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:57.050
I'm last.

00:15:57.410 --> 00:15:59.400
Guess what this is!

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:03.490
No matter what side I look 
at it from, I have no idea.

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:05.930
It's almost like folded cloth.

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:09.940
The right answer was the 
skull of a hammerhead shark!

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:12.820
So it has bones all the way 
to the edges of its head.

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:16.630
It's fun to think about animals
 by looking at their bones!

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:19.670
Could I ask you to start from 
the bones for your next job?

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:21.070
Our next job?

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:25.550
Yes! After you submitted that large demon,

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:28.710
I wanted to ask you to make 
a small messenger familiar.

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:30.960
Something like this.

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:34.140
If you like, we could 
start brainstorming now.

00:16:34.730 --> 00:16:36.730
Are you sure? It is your day off.

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:40.050
It's fun to think with a buzz sometimes.

00:16:40.050 --> 00:16:42.930
The less work <i>feels</i> like work,
 the more fun it is.

00:16:42.930 --> 00:16:43.970
Same.

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:48.620
All right, could you tell us about 
this familiar's tasks and purpose?

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:50.370
The workplace will be underground!

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:54.860
<b>Hell Interior</b>

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:52.030
Since they will be messengers,

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:54.130
they should have amazing hearing 
and be quick on their feet.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:57.740
<b>Familiar Waiting Room</b>

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:57.730
I'd like them to be able to communicate
 in a unique way, without sound.

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:57.740
<b>Employee Passageway</b>

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:02.510
There will be many operational messages 
that we don't want our guests to hear.

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:07.070
Yes, fast like lightning! When they stop, 
they should be like the night fog!

00:17:07.070 --> 00:17:08.880
Something like that would be ideal.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:11.270
<i>As always, a unique way 
of expressing himself.</i>

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:17.130
And also, if they were to rest in front 
of our guests, we might get complaints,

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:21.170
so it would be good if it's not easy to tell 
if they're awake or sleeping at first glance.

00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:24.280
Even in Hell, they try to
 avoid customer complaints.

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:27.780
If that's the case, we also have to 
think about its toilet breaks, too.

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:30.650
Oh, I didn't think about that.

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:34.200
That's solved if they just eat the 
poop straight from their own butt.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:37.470
Are you taking things too far already?

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:40.790
It's not a joke. I mean koalas eat poop, too.

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:44.200
<b>For Eating</b>

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:44.200
<b>Not for Eating</b>

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:44.540
Koalas have two kinds of poop.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:50.630
<b>For Eating</b>

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:47.230
Indigestible waste is not for eating,

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:50.820
while the medicine-like stuff that 
the caecum creates is for eating.

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:53.780
The koala poop that's for eating is healthy.

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:56.110
That's why their baby food 
after weaning is poop.

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:59.510
The idea that they can create 
their own medicine is great!

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:03.820
I would like to use that. 
We need our staff to be healthy.

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:07.890
All right, if we put that all together...
Something like this?

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:14.280
A casual scariness fit for a familiar! Nice!

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:18.660
In order to specialize in speed, I gave 
them a single bone below the knee.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.090
With two bones, the leg can twist,

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:24.340
but fusing those into one 
makes it more powerful.

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:27.670
With these legs, they can go up
 to eighty kilometers per hour.

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:29.840
So much thought goes into unseen places!

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:32.830
Since your order was so detailed 
and easy to understand,

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:34.720
it's already done.

00:18:35.140 --> 00:18:37.180
Do you want to work on 
the exterior look now?

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:40.290
We don't have to push it now. 
You can finish it when you get a chance.

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.560
What's wrong, Neptune-san?

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:47.980
No, it's just that I realized how 
much fun creating things can be.

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:50.010
He's in a slump right now.

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:51.950
He's worn out.

00:18:52.890 --> 00:18:56.860
Then how about creating something freely?

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:01.320
If you unshackle your instincts 
and draw for your own enjoyment,

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:02.940
you might be able to reset yourself.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:05.220
How about this?

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:09.380
Would you mind coming up with the 
exterior look for these bones here?

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:14.260
I want to see what you create when 
you're uninhibited and playful.

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:18.600
Freely? Enjoy myself?

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:23.510
<i>Neptune-san picked up his pen!</i>

00:19:24.190 --> 00:19:26.250
<i>Yokota-senpai is amazing.</i>

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:28.940
<i>I couldn't get him to do that.</i>

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:31.520
<i>One day, I'll also...</i>

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:33.240
Done!

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:35.890
What do you think?

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:47.400
Hey, why did something 
scary turn into this?!

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:49.170
That was so much fun.

00:19:49.590 --> 00:19:53.910
So he put those long bones 
into this round tail?

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:58.070
This super-cute thing... eats poop?

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:00.240
And sleeps with its eyes open?

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:01.420
What are these ears?

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:06.230
They're heat sinks. Since I increased 
its muscle mass for running fast,

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:08.330
I thought it might overheat and collapse.

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:12.050
They also double as sound collecting 
antennae for picking up orders from far away.

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:16.920
How did you solve the request for the 
unique non-verbal communication method?

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:20.070
I made them good at sensing vibrations.

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:23.440
That way they can use foot 
stomps to communicate.

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:21.820
<b>Stomp</b>

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:28.940
Hm, isn't this more like that 
mystery order that got you down?

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:31.920
You mean the "fluffy but spiky animal."

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:34.140
Wouldn't this be a perfect fit?

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:39.340
I see! This came out because you've 
been thinking about it the whole time.

00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:43.620
From Hell's point of view, 
this design would be acceptable, too...

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:44.850
It is?

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:47.760
But if there's already a prior taker,
 then we have no choice.

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:50.280
Please deliver it to God.

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:51.070
All right!

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:57.210
Oh, Hell's outside of God's reception range.

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:59.980
What should we do? I want 
to deliver this right away.

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:04.350
Don't worry. I've invited God here, too.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:06.470
His arrival is imminent.

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:09.250
The client's coming here in person?!

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:13.610
Wait! Neptune-san faked 
being sick to come here!

00:21:13.610 --> 00:21:14.740
Our lie will be discovered!

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:21.700
Th-This light! Is this...

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:23.910
God?!

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:30.140
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:28.900
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:33.680
They look so cute, but they eat poop.

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:37.390
They eat special vitamin-rich 
poop like a supplement,

00:21:37.390 --> 00:21:39.450
or at least that was the original plan.

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:40.760
Oh?

00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:43.240
When I observed wild rabbits,

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:45.840
they also just ate regular poop when 
there was no food to be found.

00:21:45.840 --> 00:21:48.820
So tough! In a way, if you 
eat what you excrete,

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:51.090
you're like a perpetual motion device.

00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:54.550
In winter, when there was no grass, 
they also ate animal carcasses.

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:56.160
Truly tough!

00:21:56.400 --> 00:22:01.160
Speaking of tough, when the female 
picks a male, she first punches him.

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:04.440
She makes sure the male is 
strong by punching him.

00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:07.180
Throw hands, then throw kisses!

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:08.440
How strong!

00:22:08.670 --> 00:22:11.780
Some day soon, these bunnies may be seen

00:22:11.780 --> 00:22:14.510
not as symbols of cuteness, but of strength.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:46.440
<b>Next on the Agenda</b>
